#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:281
msgid "Parser config"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:283
msgid ""
"Parser construction (i.e. `dashdash.createParser(CONFIG)`) takes the "
"following fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:286
msgid ""
"`options` (Array of option specs). Required. See the [Option specs"
"](#option-specs) section below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:289
msgid ""
"`interspersed` (Boolean). Optional. Default is true. If true this allows "
"interspersed arguments and options. I.e.:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:294
msgid ""
"Set it to false to have '-h' **not** get parsed as an option in the above"
" example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:297
msgid ""
"`allowUnknown` (Boolean).  Optional.  Default is false.  If false, this "
"causes unknown arguments to throw an error.  I.e.:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:302
msgid "Set it to true to treat the unknown option as a positional argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:305
msgid ""
"**Caveat**: When a shortopt group, such as `-xaz` contains a mix of known"
" and unknown options, the *entire* group is passed through unmolested as "
"a positional argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:309
msgid ""
"Consider if you have a known short option `-a`, and parse the following "
"command line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:314
msgid ""
"where `-x` and `-z` are unknown.  There are multiple ways to interpret "
"this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:317
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`-x` takes a value: `{x: 'az'}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:318
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`-x` and `-z` are both booleans: `{x:true,a:true,z:true}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:320
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Since dashdash does not know what `-x` and `-z` are, it can't know if "
"you'd prefer to receive `{a:true,_args:['-x','-z']}` or `{x:'az'}`, or "
"`{_args:['-xaz']}`. Leaving the positional arg unprocessed is the easiest"
" mistake for the user to recover from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:326
msgid "Option specs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:328
msgid "Example using all fields (required fields are noted):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:343
msgid ""
"Each option spec in the `options` array must/can have the following "
"fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:345
msgid ""
"`name` (String) or `names` (Array). Required. These give the option name "
"and aliases. The first name (if more than one given) is the key for the "
"parsed `opts` object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:349
msgid "`type` (String). Required. One of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:351
msgid "bool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:352
msgid "string"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:353
msgid "number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:354
msgid "integer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:355
msgid "positiveInteger"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:356
msgid ""
"date (epoch seconds, e.g. 1396031701, or ISO 8601 format `YYYY-MM-"
"DD[THH:MM:SS[.sss][Z]]`, e.g. \"2014-03-28T18:35:01.489Z\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:358
msgid "arrayOfBool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:359
msgid "arrayOfString"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:360
msgid "arrayOfNumber"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:361
msgid "arrayOfInteger"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:362
msgid "arrayOfPositiveInteger"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:363
msgid "arrayOfDate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:365
msgid ""
"FWIW, these names attempt to match with asserts on [assert-"
"plus](https://github.com/mcavage/node-assert-plus). You can add your own "
"custom option types with `dashdash.addOptionType`. See below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:370
msgid ""
"`completionType` (String). Optional. This is used for [Bash completion"
"](#bash-completion) for an option argument. If not specified, then the "
"value of `type` is used. Any string may be specified, but only the "
"following values have meaning:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:375
msgid "`none`: Provide no completions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:376
msgid ""
"`file`: Bash's default completion (i.e. `complete -o default`), which "
"includes filenames."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:378
msgid ""
"*Any string FOO for which a `function complete_FOO` Bash function is "
"defined.* This is for custom completions for a given tool. Typically "
"these custom functions are provided in the `specExtra` argument to "
"`dashdash.bashCompletionFromOptions()`. See "
"[\"examples/ddcompletion.js\"](examples/ddcompletion.js) for an example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:384
msgid ""
"`env` (String or Array of String). Optional. An environment variable name"
" (or names) that can be used as a fallback for this option. For example, "
"given a \"foo.js\" like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:391
msgid ""
"Both `node foo.js --dry-run` and `FOO_DRY_RUN=1 node foo.js` would result"
" in `opts.dry_run = true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:394
msgid ""
"An environment variable is only used as a fallback, i.e. it is ignored if"
" the associated option is given in `argv`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:397
msgid "`help` (String). Optional. Used for `parser.help()` output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:399
msgid ""
"`helpArg` (String). Optional. Used in help output as the placeholder for "
"the option argument, e.g. the \"PATH\" in:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:406
msgid ""
"`helpWrap` (Boolean). Optional, default true. Set this to `false` to have"
" that option's `help` *not* be text wrapped in `<parser>.help()` output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:409
msgid ""
"`default`. Optional. A default value used for this option, if the option "
"isn't specified in argv."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:412
msgid ""
"`hidden` (Boolean). Optional, default false. If true, help output will "
"not include this option. See also the `includeHidden` option to "
"`bashCompletionFromOptions()` for [Bash completion](#bash-completion)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:417
msgid "Option group headings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:419
msgid ""
"You can add headings between option specs in the `options` array.  To do "
"so, simply add an object with only a `group` property -- the string to "
"print as the heading for the subsequent options in the array.  For "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:443
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Note: You can use an empty string, `{group: ''}`, to get a blank line in "
"help output between groups of options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:447
msgid "Help config"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:449
msgid "The `parser.help(...)` function is configurable as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:461
msgid ""
"`indent` (Number or String). Default 4. Set to a number (for that many "
"spaces) or a string for the literal indent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:463
msgid ""
"`headingIndent` (Number or String). Default half length of `indent`. Set "
"to a number (for that many spaces) or a string for the literal indent. "
"This indent applies to group heading lines, between normal option lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:466
msgid ""
"`nameSort` (String). Default is 'length'. By default the names are sorted"
" to put the short opts first (i.e. '-h, --help' preferred to '--help, "
"-h'). Set to 'none' to not do this sorting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:469
msgid ""
"`maxCol` (Number). Default 80. Note that reflow is just done on "
"whitespace so a long token in the option help can overflow maxCol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:471
msgid ""
"`helpCol` (Number). If not set a reasonable value will be determined "
"between `minHelpCol` and `maxHelpCol`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:473
msgid "`minHelpCol` (Number). Default 20."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:474
msgid "`maxHelpCol` (Number). Default 40."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:475
msgid ""
"`helpWrap` (Boolean). Default true. Set to `false` to have option `help` "
"strings *not* be textwrapped to the helpCol..maxCol range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:477
msgid ""
"`includeEnv` (Boolean). Default false. If the option has associated "
"environment variables (via the `env` option spec attribute), then append "
"mentioned of those envvars to the help string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:480
msgid ""
"`includeDefault` (Boolean). Default false. If the option has a default "
"value (via the `default` option spec attribute, or a default on the "
"option's type), then a \"Default: VALUE\" string will be appended to the "
"help string."
msgstr ""

