#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:542
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:544
msgid "Why another node.js option parsing lib?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:546
msgid ""
"`nopt` really is just for \"tools like npm\". Implicit opts (e.g. '--no-"
"foo' works for every '--foo'). Can't disable abbreviated opts. Can't do "
"multiple usages of same opt, e.g. '-vvv' (I think). Can't do grouped "
"short opts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:550
msgid ""
"`optimist` has surprise interpretation of options (at least to me). "
"Implicit opts mean ambiguities and poor error handling for fat-fingering."
" `process.exit` calls makes it hard to use as a libary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:554
msgid ""
"`optparse` Incomplete docs. Is this an attempted clone of Python's "
"`optparse`. Not clear. Some divergence. `parser.on(\"name\", ...)` API is"
" weird."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:557
msgid ""
"`argparse` Dep on underscore. No thanks just for option processing. `find"
" lib | wc -l` -> `26`. Overkill. Argparse is a bit different anyway. Not "
"sure I want that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:561
msgid ""
"`posix-getopt` No type validation. Though that isn't a killer. AFAIK "
"can't have a long opt without a short alias. I.e. no `getopt_long` "
"semantics. Also, no whizbang features like generated help output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dashdash_README.md:565
msgid ""
"[\"commander.js\"](https://github.com/visionmedia/commander.js): I wrote "
"[a critique](http://trentm.com/2014/01/a-critique-of-commander-for-"
"nodejs.html) a while back. It seems fine, but last I checked had [an "
"outstanding bug](https://github.com/visionmedia/commander.js/pull/121) "
"that would prevent me from using it."
msgstr ""

